  "query_preview": "(Monday through Thursday)...\nWarming of high temperatures of a few degrees per day for inland\nareas will continue through Tuesday with not much change on\nWednesday and slight cooling on Thursday. High temperatures for\nTuesday and Wednesday will be within a few degrees of average for\nmost areas with the lower deserts around 5 degrees above average.\nHigh temperatures will range from the mid 70s to around 80 near\nthe coast to the 90s to around 100 for the Inland Empire with 108\nto 112 for the lower deserts.\n\nDry weather will continue through next week. The marine layer will\nbecome slightly shallower through the middle of next week with \nnight and morning coastal low clouds spreading inland into the far\nwestern valleys at times.",
